Title: test_docs.sh must fail on stale generated manual (docs drift guard)
Created: 2026-06-04
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-06-04T10:36Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context
Surfaced by /verify on PR #269 (raid 219-224, ticket 0220): the PR
changed helpMigrate but the committed docs/erg-manual.md (a tracked
generated handoff artifact) was stale -- the execute agent ran
`make docs` but forgot to commit the output. CI did not catch it:
tests/test_docs.sh only checks the manual is non-empty, never that
it is current. The verify gate caught it empirically (REROLL round 1)
and committed the regen; without that gate the stale manual would
have merged.

## Actions
1. Add a drift check to tests/test_docs.sh: regenerate the manual
   (make docs or the underlying command) into a temp file and diff
   against the committed docs/erg-manual.md; fail on any difference.

## Test
With a deliberately edited (stale) docs/erg-manual.md, the suite
fails; after `make docs`, it passes.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] test_docs.sh fails when docs/erg-manual.md is stale against
      the binary's help text
- [ ] Suite remains offline (no network) and hermetic
- [ ] make check passes
